<title>USA: Gander Mountain to sell assets to Holiday.</title>
<headline>Gander Mountain to sell assets to Holiday.</headline>
<dateline>WILMOT, Wis. 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gander Moutnain Inc, which went into Chapter 11 bankruptcy in August, said Tuesday that Holiday Cos agreed to buy all its assets, including 12 retail stores.</p>
<p>Bloomington, Minnesota-based Holiday Cos will assume all of Gander's secured debt, administrative expenses of the bankruptcy and priority claims. It will also pay $19.5 million.</p>
<p>Of that amount, $18.5 million would go to unsecured creditors, $500,000 to preferred stockholders and $500,000 to common stockholders.</p>
</text>
